        "# iterations. This shows that the estimated model is quickly adjusting to minimize\n",
        "# the difference between the observed pseudoranges and computed ranges. As the iterations\n",
        "# continue, the curve flattens. This shows that further improvements become smaller\n",
        "# once the solution is near the optimum value.\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Corrections (delta):\n",
        "# The Log of corrections are also decreasing exponentially, it means that the update\n",
        "# applied to the state vector becomes smaller each iteration. Large corrections\n",
        "# in early iterations reflect a poor initial guess, while small corrections near\n",
        "# the end indicate convergance. when the delta becomes very small, the algorithm\n",
        "# meets the stopping criterion.\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3D Position Error:\n",
        "# The position error against the ground truth also decreases in a similar manner, exponentially.\n",
        "# This shows that the estimated receiver position is moving closer to the true position\n",
        "# with each iteration. Once the curve stabilizes, the final position error represents\n",
        "# the accuracy of the LSE solution given the measurement noise and satellite geometry.\n",
        "\n",
        "# So overall, the patterns reflect a well-behaved iterative LSQ process, i.e., fast\n",
        "# initial improvement, diminishing updates and stable convergance."
      ]
