        "### Step 4: Test Model (3 x 3 = 9 marks)\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculate the following for the **three different tests** implemented in Step 3:\n",
        "1. data size (0.5 mark)\n",
        "2. number of training samples (0.5 mark)\n",
        "3. number of testing samples (0.5 mark)\n",
        "4. training accuracy (0.5 mark)\n",
        "5. testing accuracy (0.5 mark)\n",
        "6. log loss (0.5 mark)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 19,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, log_loss\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Data size: 27898\n",
